# C# XML Flowerbox
Whenever generating, refactoring, or documenting C# methods, always use the following "Flowerbox" XML documentation format.

## Requirements
- Include summary, param, returns
- Action-Oriented Summaries: Use concise, sentence-case descriptions (e.g., "Process Incoming Claim").
- Strict Type Referencing: For every parameter that is a complex object or custom class, you **must** include a `<see cref="TypeName" />` tag within the `<param>` description.
- Triple-Slash Consistency: Ensure all lines start with `///` and are properly indented with the method signature.
- Return Descriptions: Always include a `<returns>` tag describing the output object.

## Template

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// [Action description]
/// </summary>
/// <param name="[name]">Description <see cref="[TypeName]"/></param>
/// <returns>Description</returns>
```

